    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2-a1">

                <pb facs="0012" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg2"/>

                <head>Mr. Sprague to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Gibraltar,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 19, 1863—5½. <hi rendition="#italic">p.
                            m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The British tug-boat Lion Belge, which
                    plies between Tangier and this port, has just arrived, and her commander states
                    that there is a confederate man-of-war steamer at Cape Spartel.</p>
                <p>I forward this information to your excellency by telegraph, and also to our
                    representatives at Paris, Lisbon, Cadiz, &amp;c.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HORATIO J. SPRAGUE, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles F. Adams</hi>,, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Minister, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;.,
                            London.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
